  "result": "I revised the record for `NRS_484B_250_1` and wrote it to `record.jsonl`. It hasn't been through the gate yet. The coder still has to build the new witness and rerun the gate.\n\n**Why the gate returned VACUOUS:** no scenario reached the `NRS_484B_250_4_o2` composition, and dropping it would be wrong. The two subsection 4 rules apply at different moments:\n- **o1** applies only at the observation where x enters the intersection.\n- **o2** applies at every observation where x, having made the required stop, is moving inside the intersection. That includes observations after the entry, where o1 no longer applies.\n\nThe coder's last scenario put the conflict at the moment of entry. There o1 already lifts the \"controlled intersection\" exception, so the result never depended on o2.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **New scenario `branch_4`, expected violated.** The intersection has an inoperative signal. x halts at its stop line and enters while no other vehicle is in the intersection, so nothing is owed at the entry. At the next observation x is still moving across its approach lane and the intersection. A vehicle from the other highway has now entered, and a conflict is predicted. Only o2 lifts the exception at that observation, so without it the result would be not applicable.\n- **Applicability wording.** It now says when each subsection 4 rule lifts the exception: o1 at the entry, o2 at the entry and the moments after it.\n- **Housekeeping.** The `s3` narrowing now has `kind: \"reading\"`. The `int.turn_left` intention now uses the catalogue id without its own meaning.\n\nNothing else in the record changed: same text segments, atoms, parameters and compositions.",
